  "worked_solution": "The power set of $T,$ denoted $P(T),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $T,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that we are given the set $\u2205.$ So, its power set must be ${\u2205}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that we are given the set ${a,\u2205}.$ So, its power set must be ${\u2205,{a},{\u2205},{a,\u2205}}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the power set of the set ${\u2205}$ is ${\u2205,{\u2205}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
